<title>UK: Mexico's Axa sets $200 million seven-year bond.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Axa sets $200 million seven-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Chase.</p>
<p> BORROWER   AXA S.A DE C.V</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  ***</p>
<p> AMT    $200 MLN	COUPON     9.00	MATURITY    04.AUG.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.25     PAY DATE    04.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  75 BP     REOFFER    99.25     SPREAD	+300 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	B1	  LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  BB	  DENOMS (K) 1 (REG) 250 (144A)</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   SALE LIMS  US/UK</p>
<p> MGT/UND    25 BP     SELL CONC  50 BP</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 7.25 PCT 2004 U.S.T  NOTES    ***INDUSTRIAS AXA, AXA CABLES, CONDUCTORES CM,</p>
<p>		 AND PROLEC AND LUMSISTEMS.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
